# Append-only documents. Every pull request adds an entry at the top of these
# two, at the same anchor, so any two open branches conflict by construction —
# it happened three times in a fortnight and the resolution was identical each
# time: keep both.
#
# merge=union does exactly that. The cost is that git stops reporting a
# conflict here, so two branches editing the SAME existing line get both
# versions silently rather than a marker. These files are almost entirely
# append-only, which is what makes the trade worth taking; the one line that is
# genuinely edited rather than appended is readme.txt's "Stable tag", and
# bin/validate-config.php fails the build if union merge ever duplicates a
# single-value header there.
CHANGELOG.md    merge=union
readme.txt      merge=union

# Deliberately NOT union: languages/producerkit.pot is generated, and
# concatenating two versions of it produces a file neither branch would
# reproduce. The right resolution is always to regenerate, and
# `composer make-pot:check` fails CI on a stale one.
